<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#RegisterStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The lifecycle state of a register entry (a concept, collection or scheme). Closed set: hexplain:statusValid, hexplain:statusDeprecated, hexplain:statusSuperseded."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#RegisterStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The class of the three controlled values of hexplain:status; do not mint further statuses. A register publishes the status of its entries; data never states it."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#RegisterStatusShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A register entry states at most one lifecycle status from the closed set; a deprecated or superseded entry is owl:deprecated true, a valid one is not, and a superseded entry names its successor."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#RegisterStatusShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using hexplain:status Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
