<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#byteLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The length in bytes, from hexplain:byteOffset, of a lifted resource's physical extent."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#byteLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Stated by a processor on the resources it lifts, with hexplain:byteOffset, when it records byte ranges; a profile does not declare it. Also locates a conf:Finding's evidence."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#byteOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The zero-based byte offset, within its asset, of a lifted resource's physical extent."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#byteOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Stated by a processor on the resources it lifts, with hexplain:byteLength, when it records byte ranges; a profile does not declare it. Also locates a conf:Finding's evidence."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#codec> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The algorithm this step applies, drawn from whichever codec or compression register the profile binds -- the same registers hexplain:isEncodedWith draws on."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#codec> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use exactly once on a hexplain:EncodingStep, naming a concept of the codec or compression register the profile binds."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#codecParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A named parameter value associated with one stage of an encoding pipeline."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#codecParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use on a hexplain:EncodingStep, once per setting the codec was applied with; omit it for a codec that takes none."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#condition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A HEL boolean condition selecting a semantic mapping or conditional class mapping in its declared context."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#condition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use exactly once on a hexplain:MappingRule or hexplain:ClassMappingRule: a HEL Boolean expression evaluated in the context of the field or struct being mapped."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#correspondsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Links a register concept to the ontology individual that names the same thing in another layer (for example a checksum-register concept to the bddo:ChecksumAlgorithm individual a physical description uses). An annotation, not a SKOS mapping and not owl:sameAs: it asserts no equivalence between a concept and an individual and licenses no inference; tools use it to keep the two identifiers aligned."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#correspondsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use on a register concept to name the ontology individual that denotes the same thing in another layer (a checksum concept and its bddo:ChecksumAlgorithm). It is an annotation: never a SKOS mapping, never equivalence, and it licenses no inference."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#forProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The semantic RDF predicate whose controlled-value register binding is declared by this binding resource."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#forProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use exactly once on a hexplain:RegisterBinding, naming the property whose values the binding constrains."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasConditionalClassMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered rdf:List of hexplain:ClassMappingRule on a bddo:Struct. The class the Struct maps to is the hexplain:semanticClass of the first rule whose hexplain:condition holds — modelling tagged unions and variant records, where a record's type depends on a discriminator field. Mutually exclusive with hexplain:mapsToClass."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasConditionalClassMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Struct whose class depends on a discriminator; its object is an rdf:List of hexplain:ClassMappingRule. Do not combine with hexplain:mapsToClass on the same struct."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasConditionalMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An ordered list of mapping rules that choose a semantic property according to the parsed instance."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasConditionalMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Field whose meaning depends on a discriminator; its object is an rdf:List of hexplain:MappingRule, the first matching rule deciding the property and value emitted."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasDataLayout> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a bddo:Field to a dlv:DataLayout describing its multi-dimensional interpretation."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasDataLayout> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Field whose bytes are a multi-dimensional array, naming the dlv:DataLayout that addresses its cells."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasEncodingStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ordered rdf:List of EncodingStep, in the order the ENCODER applied them; a decoder inverts them in reverse. Mutually exclusive with hexplain:isEncodedWith, which remains the shorthand for a single unparameterised codec."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#hasEncodingStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Field whose bytes pass through a pipeline of codecs; its object is an rdf:List of hexplain:EncodingStep in encoding order. Do not combine with hexplain:isEncodedWith."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#isEncodedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The algorithm needed to interpret a data block, drawn from whichever codec or compression register the profile binds. A processor decodes the block, then re-parses the decoded bytes against the field's data type when it is a bddo:Struct."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#isEncodedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Field whose bytes are encoded by a single codec without parameters. For several codecs or parameterised ones, use hexplain:hasEncodingStep instead."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#language> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A fixed BCP-47 language tag applied to the string literal emitted for a bddo:Field, producing a language-tagged literal. Mutually exclusive with hexplain:languageFromField."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#language> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Field that emits a string literal, with a BCP 47 tag fixed by the format. Do not combine with hexplain:languageFromField."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#languageFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The bddo:Field whose parsed string value supplies the BCP-47 language tag for this field's emitted string literal, for formats that carry a text run's language in a sibling field. Mutually exclusive with hexplain:language."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#languageFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Field whose language the data states in a sibling field, naming that field. Do not combine with hexplain:language."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToClass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a bddo:Struct to the owl:Class it physically represents."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToClass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Struct, naming the owl:Class every parsed instance of it is typed with. Use hexplain:hasConditionalClassMapping when the class depends on a discriminator."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToObjectProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a bddo:Field to the owl:ObjectProperty whose object is an IRI rather than a literal: the resource minted for a nested Struct instance (when the field's bddo:dataType is a bddo:Struct) or the field's enumeration symbol IRI (when it carries a bddo:enumeration whose bddo:enumSymbol values are IRIs). Use hexplain:mapsToProperty for literal-valued fields and this property for IRI-valued edges, so that a described format yields a connected RDF graph rather than isolated literals."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToObjectProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Field whose emitted object is an IRI: a nested struct's resource or an enumeration symbol. Use hexplain:mapsToProperty for a literal value."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a bddo:Field to the rdf:Property it supplies a value for."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#mapsToProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use on a bddo:Field that emits a literal, naming the property the literal is the value of."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#parameterName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The setting's name as the codec itself names it: \"clevel\", \"shuffle\", \"predictor\"."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#parameterName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use exactly once on a hexplain:CodecParameter."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#parameterValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The setting's value, as the literal the format carries. Left untyped: a level is an integer, a Blosc inner codec a string, a flag a boolean."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#parameterValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use exactly once on a hexplain:CodecParameter, as the literal the format carries, with the datatype that literal naturally has."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#register> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The skos:ConceptScheme whose members are the permitted values."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#register> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use exactly once on a hexplain:RegisterBinding, naming the skos:ConceptScheme whose members are permitted values of the bound property."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#semanticClass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The owl:Class selected by a hexplain:ClassMappingRule when its condition holds."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#semanticClass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use exactly once on a hexplain:ClassMappingRule, naming the class chosen when its condition holds."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#semanticProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The RDF property selected by a matching semantic mapping rule."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#semanticProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use exactly once on a hexplain:MappingRule, naming the property emitted when its condition holds."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#status> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The lifecycle state of a register entry. Absent means valid for an entry that is not owl:deprecated."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#status> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a register entry (a concept, collection or scheme) that a register retires or reaffirms. A deprecated or superseded entry is also owl:deprecated true and has a history note; a superseded one names its replacement with dcterms:isReplacedBy."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#statusDeprecated> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The entry is retained for existing data but SHOULD NOT be used in new data; there is no single successor. It carries owl:deprecated true and a skos:historyNote."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#statusDeprecated> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use as the hexplain:status of a retired register entry that has no single replacement."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#statusSuperseded> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The entry is retained for existing data and replaced by the entry or entries named with dcterms:isReplacedBy, which new data SHOULD use. It carries owl:deprecated true and a skos:historyNote."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#statusSuperseded> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use as the hexplain:status of a retired register entry that names its replacement with dcterms:isReplacedBy."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#statusValid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The entry is current. An entry with no hexplain:status is valid unless it is owl:deprecated."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#statusValid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use as the hexplain:status of a current register entry, where saying so explicitly helps; an entry with no status is current unless it is owl:deprecated."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#unit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The unit of measure of the quantity a bddo:Field carries, as an IRI drawn from a unit vocabulary (e.g. QUDT or UCUM; the range is skos:Concept but any unit IRI is permitted). Annotation only: it records the physical unit of the emitted value and does not rescale it — use hexplain:valueExpression for numeric conversion."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#unit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Field whose value is a quantity, naming its unit of measure. It records the unit; it does not rescale the value."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#usesRegister> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Binds a property used by this profile to the register supplying its values."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#usesRegister> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use on the profile, once per property it binds to a register; the object is a hexplain:RegisterBinding."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#valueDatatype> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The xsd datatype of a computed hexplain:valueExpression result; defaults to the natural datatype of the HEL result type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#valueDatatype> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once beside a hexplain:valueExpression, naming the datatype of the literal it emits when the HEL result's natural datatype is not the one wanted."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#valueExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A HEL expression computing the value to emit for the mapped property instead of the field's raw parsed value (e.g. fixed-point or unit scaling). Evaluated in the field's context."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/core#valueExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use at most once on a bddo:Field or a hexplain:MappingRule, when the emitted value is computed from the parsed one (scaling, offsets, unit conversion) rather than copied."@en .
